ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049763 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050819 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186115209 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050819 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186115210 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050819 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186115211 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050819 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186115212 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050819 #edb/ref 1031 "The Sum and Constant Multiple Rules for Definite Integrals" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050819 #edb/ref 1033 1685 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050819 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "68fac9fb-a6fb-5c4b-a510-881f3f9dcbd6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050929 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048169 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050929 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048569 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050929 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048685 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050929 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049050 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050929 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049374 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050929 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049433 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050929 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050289 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050929 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050355 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050929 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050521 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050929 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050787 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050929 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186064245 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050929 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186064246 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050929 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186064274 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050929 #edb/ref 1031 "Introduction to Integration by Parts" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050929 #edb/ref 1033 317 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050929 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "7280f087-059d-5524-8f8b-a1fe79b4ef9d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050989 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186166960 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050989 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186166961 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050989 #edb/ref 1031 "Convergence of Fourier Series" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050989 #edb/ref 1033 3198 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050989 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "7742668d-ad15-5c25-bc82-4ea5b4fd800d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186221196 #edb/ref 1069 "e-21835" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186221196 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $f(x)$ be the $2L$-periodic extension of a function $F(x)$ from $x\\in [-L,L)$ to $x \\in \\mathbb R.$ \nGiven that $L=2$ and $f(x) = \\cosh{(x+1)}$, find the $4$th cosine and the $4$th sine coefficients." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186221196 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b8658f47-7f42-530a-a62e-1cc3144059aa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186221196 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that multiplying the argument of a function by $k \\neq 0$ represents the horizontal stretching of the corresponding graph by a factor of $\\dfrac{1}{k}.$\n\nNow, let $s=\\dfrac{\\pi}{L}x.$ Then, since $f(x)$ has a period of $2L,$ the function\n\n$$\ng(s) = f\\left(\\dfrac{L}{\\pi}s\\right)\n$$\n\nmust have a period of $2L \\cdot \\dfrac{\\pi}{L} = 2\\pi.$ \n\nThe Fourier series of $g(s)$ is\n\n$$\ng(s) \\sim \\dfrac{a_0}{2}+\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty}a_n\\cos(ns)+b_n\\sin(ns),\n$$\n\nwhere:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{0} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }g(s)\\,\\text{d}s \\\\ {a}_{n} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }g(s)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(ns)\\,\\text{d}s,\\,n\\ge 1 \\\\ {b}_{n} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }g(s)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(ns)\\,\\text{d}s,\\,n\\ge 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $s=\\dfrac{\\pi}{L}x$ and using the fact that $g(s) = f\\left(\\dfrac{L}{\\pi}s\\right),$ we get the Fourier series of $f(x){:}$\n\n$$\nf(x) \\sim \\dfrac{a_0}{2}+\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty}\na_n\\cos\\bigg(\\bbox[4pt, border: solid 1pt gainsboro]{\\dfrac{n\\pi}{L}x}\\bigg)+\nb_n\\sin\\bigg(\\bbox[4pt, border: solid 1pt gainsboro]{\\dfrac{n\\pi}{L}x}\\bigg)\n$$\n\nTherefore, $4$th cosine coefficient of $f(x)$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{4} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }g(s)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4s)\\,\\text{d}s \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(\\frac{L}{\\pi }s)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4s)\\,\\text{d}s \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-L}^{L}f(\\frac{L}{\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{L}x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{L}x)\\,\\text{d}(\\frac{\\pi }{L}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{L}{\\int }_{-L}^{L}f(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{4\\pi }{L}x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{L}{\\int }_{-L}^{L}f(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{4\\pi }{L}x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, $4$th sine coefficient of $f(x)$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{4} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }g(s)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4s)\\,\\text{d}s \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(\\frac{L}{\\pi }s)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4s)\\,\\text{d}s \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-L}^{L}f(\\frac{L}{\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{L}x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{L}x)\\,\\text{d}(\\frac{\\pi }{L}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{L}{\\int }_{-L}^{L}f(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{4\\pi }{L}x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{L}{\\int }_{-L}^{L}f(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{4\\pi }{L}x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $L=2$ and $f(x)=\\cosh(x+1),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{4} & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(x+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{4\\pi }{2}x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(x+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi x)\\,\\text{d}x, \\\\ {b}_{4} & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(x+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{4\\pi }{2}x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(x+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186221197 #edb/ref 1069 "e-21836" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186221197 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\nf(x) \\sim \\dfrac{a_0}{2}+\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty}a_n\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{n\\pi}{2}x\\right)+b_n\\sin\\left(\\dfrac{n\\pi}{2}x\\right)\n$$\n\nLet $F(x)=3x^2-4x+1$ for $x\\in[-2,2).$ The Fourier series of the $4$-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ is shown above. Find the exact value of $a_0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186221197 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ba1cc59e-66ed-58fc-a494-b949c7ed0a88" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186221197 #edb/ref 1074 "For the Fourier series of a $2L$-periodic function, the constant term is given by\n\n$$\na_0=\\frac{1}{L}\\int_{-L}^{L} f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $L=2$ and $f(x)=3x^2-4x+1$ for $x \\in [-2,2).$ So, substituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{0} & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}(3{x}^{2}-4x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{[{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+x]}_{-2}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(({2}^{3}-2\\cdot {2}^{2}+2)-((-2)^{3}-2\\cdot (-2)^{2}+(-2))) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(2-(-18)) \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186221198 #edb/ref 1069 "e-21837" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186221198 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\nf(x) \\sim \\dfrac{a_0}{2}+\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty}a_n\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{n\\pi}{2}x\\right)+b_n\\sin\\left(\\dfrac{n\\pi}{2}x\\right)\n$$\n\nLet $F(x)=-5x+4$ for $x\\in[-2,2).$ The Fourier series of the $4$-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ is shown above. Find the exact value of $a_3.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186221198 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "823fc00b-48af-5e79-9dcc-5e519e81cd4f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186221198 #edb/ref 1074 "For the Fourier series of a $2L$-periodic function, the cosine coefficients are given by\n\n$$\na_n=\\frac{1}{L}\\int_{-L}^{L} f(x)\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{n\\pi}{L}x\\right)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $L=2$ and $f(x)=-5x+4$ for $x \\in [-2,2).$ So, substituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\na_3 = \\dfrac{1}{2}\\int_{-2}^{2} (-5x+4)\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{3\\pi}{2}x\\right)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe use the integration by parts: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=-5x+4\\, & ⇒\\,{u}^{′}=-5 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2}x)\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\frac{2}{3\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2}x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{3} & =\\frac{1}{2}(uv\\,{|}_{-2}^{2}-{\\int }_{-2}^{2}v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{2}{3\\pi }{[(-5x+4)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2}x)]}_{-2}^{2}-{\\int }_{-2}^{2}\\frac{2}{3\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2}x)\\cdot (-5)\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{2}{3\\pi }[(-5(2)+4)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\pi )-(-5(-2)+4)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-3\\pi )]+\\frac{10}{3\\pi }{\\int }_{-2}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2}x)\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{2}{3\\pi }\\cdot 0+\\frac{10}{3\\pi }\\cdot (-\\frac{2}{3\\pi }){[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2}x)]}_{-2}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(-\\frac{20}{9{\\pi }^{2}}[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-3\\pi )]) \\\\  & =-\\frac{10}{9{\\pi }^{2}}(-1-(-1)) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186221443 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049306 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186221443 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050676 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186221443 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186222018 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186221443 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186222028 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186221443 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186317176 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186221443 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186317177 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186221443 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186423254 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186221443 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186423255 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186221443 #edb/ref 1039 "Identifying Effects of the Horizontal Scaling on Coefficients" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186221443 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186221196 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186221443 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "12ff3452-19b6-56