257889" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372794 #edb/ref 1074 "For the Fourier series of a $2L$-periodic function, the constant term is given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{0}=\\frac{1}{L}{\\int }_{-L}^{L}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $L=6$ and $f(x)=2{x}^{2}+7x+5$ for $x\\in [-6,6).$ So, substituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{0} & =\\frac{1}{6}{\\int }_{-6}^{6}(2{x}^{2}+7x+5)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}{[\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3}+\\frac{7}{2}{x}^{2}+5x]}_{-6}^{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}((\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot {6}^{3}+\\frac{7}{2}\\cdot {6}^{2}+5\\cdot 6)-(\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot (-6)^{3}+\\frac{7}{2}\\cdot (-6)^{2}+5\\cdot (-6))) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}(300-(-48)) \\\\  & =58.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372795 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372796 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372795 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372795 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372795 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186372796 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372795 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "66bca651-fc67-586c-a6ac-fc1254c6e1f1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372796 #edb/ref 1080 "58" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372796 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372796 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "8c493bcc-7040-54a8-b5d3-429d4cf6c165" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423194 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{6L}{\\pi }x)\\,\\text{d}x" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423194 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423194 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "00561c08-ad3b-5d9b-ac8d-d1c849b75bfa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423195 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{L}{\\int }_{-L}^{L}f(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)\\,\\text{d}x" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423195 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423195 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0123e789-200e-5356-9457-fcfe3958ad6